  "body": "## Description\nThe `TokenWrapper` contract implements the ERC20 `IERC20` interface but its `transferFrom` function emits a `Transfer` event with `msg.sender` as the `from` address instead of the actual token holder (`from` parameter).  \nPer the ERC20 specification, the `Transfer` event for `transferFrom` must use the address whose balance is being debited as the first argument (`from`), not the caller (`msg.sender`).  \nThis causes emitted logs to misrepresent who actually sent tokens, making event-based balance reconstruction or monitoring incorrect.\n\n## Impact\n- Off‑chain indexers, analytics tools, and block explorers that rely on `Transfer(from, to, value)` to track balances or movements will attribute transfers to the approved spender instead of the actual token owner when `transferFrom` is used.  \n- Wallets and UIs that display token history from events will show misleading information about who sent tokens.  \n- Any off‑chain or cross‑chain infrastructure that reconstructs balances purely from events (without querying `balanceOf`) will compute incorrect balances for this wrapper token when allowances are used.  \n- No direct on‑chain loss of funds occurs, but ERC20 non‑compliance can break ecosystem integrations and developer expectations around standard behavior.\n\n## Recommendation\nUpdate `transferFrom` to emit the correct `from` address in the `Transfer` event:\n\n```solidity\n// before\nemit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount);\n\n// after\nemit Transfer(from, to, amount);\n```\n\nThis aligns the implementation with the ERC20 standard and ensures that event logs correctly reflect token flows for all indexers and external integrations.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## PoC Description\n\nThe PoC demonstrates that when Bob calls `transferFrom(alice, carol, amount)` to transfer Alice's tokens to Carol, the emitted `Transfer` event incorrectly shows `bob` (msg.sender) as the `from` address instead of `alice` (the actual token holder whose balance is debited).\n\n## PoC Code\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {IERC20} from \"forge-std/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {Test, console, Vm} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {FullTest} from \"./FullTest.sol\";\nimport {TokenWrapper} from \"../src/TokenWrapper.sol\";\nimport {TokenWrapperFactory} from \"../src/TokenWrapperFactory.sol\";\nimport {TestToken} from \"./TestToken.sol\";\nimport {BaseLocker} from \"../src/base/BaseLocker.sol\";\nimport {ICore} from \"../src/interfaces/ICore.sol\";\nimport {FlashAccountantLib} from \"../src/libraries/FlashAccountantLib.sol\";\n\ncontract TransferFromEventBugTest is FullTest {\n    TokenWrapperFactory factory;\n    TokenWrapperPeripheryForTest periphery;\n    TestToken underlying;\n\n    address alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n    address bob = makeAddr(\"bob\");  \n    address carol = makeAddr(\"carol\");\n\n    event Transfer(address indexed from, address indexed to, uint256 value);\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        FullTest.setUp();\n        underlying = new TestToken(address(this));\n        factory = new TokenWrapperFactory(core);\n        periphery = new TokenWrapperPeripheryForTest(core);\n    }\n\n    function test_POC_TransferFromEmitsWrongFromAddress() public {\n        TokenWrapper wrapper = factory.deployWrapper(IERC20(address(underlying)), 0);\n        uint256 amount = 1e18;\n\n        underlying.transfer(alice, amount);\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        underlying.approve(address(periphery), amount);\n        periphery.wrap(wrapper, uint128(amount));\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        wrapper.approve(bob, amount);\n\n        vm.startPrank(bob);\n        vm.recordLogs();\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, carol, amount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        Vm.Log[] memory logs = vm.getRecordedLogs();\n        bytes32 transferEventSig = keccak256(\"Transfer(address,address,uint256)\");\n        \n        address emittedFrom;\n        address emittedTo;\n        \n        for (uint i = 0; i < logs.length; i++) {\n            if (logs[i].topics[0] == transferEventSig) {\n                emittedFrom = address(uint160(uint256(logs[i].topics[1])));\n                emittedTo = address(uint160(uint256(logs[i].topics[2])));\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(alice), 0);\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(carol), amount);\n        assertEq(emittedFrom, bob);\n        assertNotEq(emittedFrom, alice);\n    }\n\n    function test_POC_ExpectEmitShowsBug() public {\n        TokenWrapper wrapper = factory.deployWrapper(IERC20(address(underlying)), 0);\n        uint256 amount = 1e18;\n\n        underlying.transfer(alice, amount);\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        underlying.approve(address(periphery), amount);\n        periphery.wrap(wrapper, uint128(amount));\n        wrapper.approve(bob, amount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        vm.expectEmit(true, true, true, true);\n        emit Transfer(bob, carol, amount);\n        wrapper.transferFrom(alice, carol, amount);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract TokenWrapperPeripheryForTest is BaseLocker {\n    using FlashAccountantLib for *;\n\n    constructor(ICore core) BaseLocker(core) {}\n\n    function wrap(TokenWrapper wrapper, uint128 amount) external {\n        lock(abi.encode(wrapper, msg.sender, msg.sender, int256(uint256(amount))));\n    }\n\n    function handleLockData(uint256, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory) {\n        (TokenWrapper wrapper, address payer, address recipient, int256 amount) =\n            abi.decode(data, (TokenWrapper, address, address, int256));\n\n        ACCOUNTANT.forward(address(wrapper), abi.encode(amount));\n        \n        if (uint128(uint256(amount)) > 0) {\n            ACCOUNTANT.withdraw(address(wrapper), recipient, uint128(uint256(amount)));\n        }\n        \n        if (uint256(amount) != 0) {\n            ACCOUNTANT.payFrom(payer, address(wrapper.UNDERLYING_TOKEN()), uint256(amount));\n        }\n        \n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Steps for PoC\n\n-  Save the PoC code to `test/TransferFromEventBug.t.sol`\n-  Run: `forge test --match-contract TransferFromEventBugTest -vvv`\n-  Observe test passes, confirming:\n   - `emittedFrom == bob` (msg.sender) \n   - `emittedFrom != alice` (actual token holder) \n-  The `Transfer` event emits `bob` instead of `alice`, violating ERC20 standard",
